# Voice / Consent Rule

Voice privacy invariants are non-negotiable.

- `RECORD_RAW_AUDIO=false` remains the safe default.
- Raw training audio requires explicit server-scoped consent and the selected capture target.
- Do not broaden capture to all speakers.
- Revoke stops future capture; do not silently erase prior artifacts unless a dedicated delete action is requested.
- Never expose raw WAVs, private transcripts, tokens, RVC weights, or local voice data.
- Do not describe training loss as human-perceived voice quality.
- Do not claim a clone is live-verified until a real human listening test occurs.
- Preserve barge-in cancellation semantics and turn-id safety.
